1
00:00:00,073 --> 00:00:04,123
...air-flow patterns and dispersion
of sunlight to make an informed choice.

2
00:00:04,286 --> 00:00:08,036
Why don't you pick at random, if you
don't like it, sit somewhere else next time?

3
00:00:08,207 --> 00:00:10,207
(Sheldon:)No, no, that's crazy.

4
00:00:11,627 --> 00:00:15,047
(Sheldon:)You go ahead and talk
while I figure it out.

5
00:00:15,923 --> 00:00:16,963
(Sheldon:)Okay.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,470
(Penny:)Here's the thing.

7
00:00:19,635 --> 00:00:23,975
(Penny:)So I've known for a while now
that Leonard has had a little crush on me...

8
00:00:24,139 --> 00:00:25,889
(Sheldon:)A little crush?

9
00:00:26,225 --> 00:00:27,475
(Sheldon:)Well, I suppose so.

10
00:00:27,643 --> 00:00:31,483
(Sheldon:)In the same way Menelaus
had a little crush on Helen of Troy.

11
00:00:32,731 --> 00:00:34,361
(Penny:)I don't really know who they are...

12
00:00:34,525 --> 00:00:37,905
(Sheldon:)- Menelaus was the brother of Agamemnon...
- Yeah, I don't care. Listen.

13
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:39,740
(Penny:)The point is...

14
00:00:39,905 --> 00:00:42,655
(Penny:)...Leonard isn't the kind of guy
I usually go out with.

15
00:00:42,825 --> 00:00:46,285
(Penny:)Leonard isn't the kind of guy
anyone usually goes out with.

16
00:00:47,204 --> 00:00:50,084
(Sheldon:)Would you be open
to rotating the couch clockwise 30 degrees?

17
00:00:50,249 --> 00:00:54,709
(Penny:)No. What I'm saying is,
Leonard might be different in a good way.

18
00:00:55,128 --> 00:00:58,258
And obviously, my usual choices
have not worked out so well.

19
00:00:58,423 --> 00:01:04,023
Your last one worked out well
for Koothrappali. He got a free iPod.

